#: includes/class-tzfd-privacy-exporter.php:54
msgid "Bookings and booking forms"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-tzfd-privacy-exporter.php:55
msgid "Each booking or form submission stores what the customer entered, such as name, email address, phone number, address, booking date and time, and the answers to the form fields. While the setting \"Store user's IP address?\" is on (it is on by default), the IP address of the request is stored with the booking too. The activity log records booking changes with the booking number, the time and the logged-in user who made the change. Booking records are kept until you delete them in Scheduling & Enquiries Manager. Calendar invitation files that contain booking details are saved in your uploads folder and are normally deleted once the email is sent."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-tzfd-privacy-exporter.php:58
msgid "Enquiries, customers and staff contacts"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-tzfd-privacy-exporter.php:59
msgid "Website enquiries store the name, email address, phone number, preferred contact method and enquiry text. Enquiry triage stores the intent, urgency and spam assessment for each enquiry, a draft quote, and a hashed IP address. Local customer records store the name, email address, phone number, address and notes you enter. The staff contact list stores the name, phone number and email address of each staff member you add. These records are kept until you delete them in Scheduling & Enquiries Manager."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-tzfd-privacy-exporter.php:63
msgid "When a client asks for a sign-in link, their email address is stored with the one-time link for 20 minutes and with their session for 2 hours. A cookie named tz_fd_portal_session holds the session token. After these times the records stop working, and WordPress removes them during its routine cleanup."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-tzfd-privacy-exporter.php:66
msgid "Missed-call texts, text replies and reminders"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-tzfd-privacy-exporter.php:67
msgid "If missed-call texts are turned on, the caller's phone number is sent to the SMS gateway you set up. The site counts texts per number for 24 hours, under a hashed key, to limit how many are sent. The missed-call log keeps only the last four digits. The callback and reply records keep the caller's full phone number, and the text-conversation records keep only a hashed key, turn count and opt-out flag. When a caller replies STOP, UNSUBSCRIBE, END, CANCEL or QUIT, the full number is added to an opt-out list kept in your WordPress options, and no more texts are sent until the caller replies START. The reminder and customer-email queues refer to bookings by number and hold the customer email address for messages that have not yet been sent. If a webhook is turned on, each booking event sends the booking details to the address you enter."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-tzfd-privacy-exporter.php:70
msgid "Captcha"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-tzfd-privacy-exporter.php:71
msgid "The captcha sets a cookie named rand_code and a temporary record. Both expire after 30 minutes."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-tzfd-privacy-exporter.php:74
msgid "Exporting and erasing"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-tzfd-privacy-exporter.php:75
msgid "The WordPress export tool includes the bookings, enquiries, enquiry triage notes, local customer records, callback and reply records, queued reminders and customer emails, and booking-assistant chats from earlier versions that match the email address requested. Records that are matched by phone number are found through the phone numbers saved against that address. The WordPress erase tool deletes these matching records, the client-portal sign-in links and sessions for that address, and the booking records that match it. Deleted records cannot be recovered. The phone-number opt-out list is kept as a WordPress option and is not matched by email address, so it is neither exported nor erased. Staff contacts are not deleted by the erase tool."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-tzfd-privacy-exporter.php:78
msgid "Deleting the plugin"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-tzfd-privacy-exporter.php:79
msgid "Deleting the plugin does not delete bookings or settings unless you add define( 'TZ_DELETE_DATA_ON_UNINSTALL', true ); to wp-config.php before you delete it. Chat photos and calendar invitation files are removed when the plugin is deleted."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-tzfd-privacy-exporter.php:86
msgid "An SMS gateway you choose, and your phone system. When a call is missed, the caller's phone number and one text message with the booking link are sent to the gateway address you enter. The plugin does not include a gateway or phone provider, so check that provider's terms and privacy policy before you turn this on."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-tzfd-privacy-exporter.php:90
msgid "A web page you name in the setup wizard for service import. The site makes one ordinary request for that page and reads its list items once. No customer data is sent. The page owner's terms and privacy policy apply."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-tzfd-privacy-exporter.php:94
msgid "A webhook endpoint you enter. Each booking created or booking status update sends a signed message with the booking details. If the endpoint does not accept it, the plugin retries, making up to 5 attempts in total. The receiving service's terms and privacy policy apply."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-tzfd-privacy-exporter.php:98
msgid "WhatsApp and SMS buttons below the booking form. These are links, not a connection: when a visitor taps one, their own phone or browser opens WhatsApp or their messaging app. The site does not contact WhatsApp."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-tzfd-privacy-exporter.php:103
msgid "Scheduling & Enquiries Manager stores the personal data below in your WordPress database. It does not create an account, collect a licence key or report usage to its author, and nothing is sent to the plugin author."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-tzfd-privacy-exporter.php:107
msgid "Outside services"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-tzfd-privacy-exporter.php:108
msgid "These services are used only when you turn them on and enter their details. The plugin does not load scripts, fonts or images from outside services on public pages."
msgstr ""

